            <ArticleTitle>[Changes of COX-2 expression in the dorsal horn of the spinal cord during formalin-induced inflammatory pain and hyperalgesia in rats].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>296-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To observe the changes of cyclooxygenase-2 (COX-2) expression and especially the time course of the changes in dorsal horn of the spinal cord during formalin-induced inflammatory pain and hyperalgesia in rats.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">COX-2 immunohistochemistry staining was used in rat formalin pain model.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Compared with control group the number and immunostaining density of COX-2 immunoreactive cells in the laminae I-VI of the dorsal horn of the spinal cord increased significantly 4 h, 1 d and 3 d after formalin injection (P &lt; 0.05). The most obvious increase was observed 1 d after the injection.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">COX-2 in the dorsal horn of the spinal cord is involved in the formalin-induced inflammatory pain and hyperalgesia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
